<http://data.silknow.org/object/3ba51706-f6cf-3a13-b1e2-5138feb2adf7>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dress fabric of brocaded silk with metal threads, Iran, 1800-1860"@en , "Dress fabric of brocaded silk with metal threads.\nWoven and brocaded silk, plain weave ground.\nWarp: light turquoise silk, indeterminable twist. Weft: silk: light turquoise, red, pink [or possibly faded red], bright green, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver-gilt strip close and open S-wound on cream and also on deep yellow silk cores, both Z-twist.\nLight turquoise ground with a repeating pattern of leafy lozenges joined by quatrefoil motifs. Each lozenge contains a large blossom and leaf and they are worked in metal thread with the plant leaves edged in bright green and the flower heads edged in red."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/6493de8c-2a4a-342f-bec4-0137f10f3a86> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Dress fabric of brocaded silk with metal threads.\nWoven and brocaded silk, plain weave ground.\nWarp: light turquoise silk, indeterminable twist. Weft: silk: light turquoise, red, pink [or possibly faded red], bright green, all indeterminable twist.\nMetal thread: silver-gilt strip close and open S-wound on cream and also on deep yellow silk cores, both Z-twist.\nLight turquoise ground with a repeating pattern of leafy lozenges joined by quatrefoil motifs. Each lozenge contains a large blossom and leaf and they are worked in metal thread with the plant leaves edged in bright green and the flower heads edged in red."@en , "Dress fabric of brocaded silk with metal threads, Iran, 1800-1860"@en ;
        ecrm:P43_has_dimension         <http://data.silknow.org/object/3ba51706-f6cf-3a13-b1e2-5138feb2adf7/dimension/2> , <http://data.silknow.org/object/3ba51706-f6cf-3a13-b1e2-5138feb2adf7/dimension/1> ;
        dc:identifier                  "T.21:67-1955" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O153893> .

